# Combo Box

Shared UI in `src/components/ComboBox.tsx`. Native `<input list>` + `<datalist>`: type to filter, pick a suggestion. Not a `<select>`.

When the user says **Combo Box**, use this component. Do not invent another autocomplete.

## Behavior

- Options are `{ id, label }`. The visible field shows **label**; a hidden `name` input submits **id**.
- Match exact label, then case-insensitive. Empty is allowed only if `allowEmpty` or not `required`.
- **Enter** commits the first remaining list option whose label contains the typed text (case-insensitive, list order; exact match wins). Does not submit a surrounding form. Native datalist cannot highlight that row. If nothing matches, Enter does nothing (`allowAny` keeps the typed text).
- Unknown typed text is **invalid while shown** (`setCustomValidity`, blocks native submit and Fit List Save). On blur it **reverts** to the last list value (or empty). Do not persist free-typed values that are not on the list.
- **`allowAny`**: typed text need not be on the list (filter name). Still offers datalist suggestions. Catalog pickers must not set `allowAny`.
- A **×** sits inside the field on the right and clears the value. The drop Combo Box in a size/drop grid passes `clearable={false}`. An outer clear wrapper hides its own button when this × is present, so the field has one ×.
- Filter dependent lists in the parent (e.g. ship-to by customer). Remount with `key` when the parent id changes.

## Use Combo Box for catalogs

Lot, model, item, size chart, brand, collection, color, pattern, content, vendor, customer, ship-to, product, import template/sheet/source header, availability **season**.

Instock stays a checkbox, not a Combo Box option.

## Keep `<select>` for short closed lists

Charge type, season period, address type, cutting/shipment status, contact kind, import template target.

Reuse this instead of a searchable custom dropdown or a long `<select>` of catalog rows.
